00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:11,120
Yeah, I mean, I think I've certainly tried spending money on design over the thirteen years.

334
00:29:11,280 --> 00:29:18,800
Like, it's not that I've never done it, but it's it it was never it never paid off for me enough that for it to be something I continue doing.

335
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:22,000
And I don't think I've done it in five, six years now.

336
00:29:23,120 --> 00:29:31,920
And at this point, the only design that I typically will ever pay for is app icon design, because that's just something that I can't do very well myself.

337
00:29:32,080 --> 00:29:34,720
We even like Widgetsmith, the icon I made myself.

338
00:29:35,120 --> 00:30:01,440
because it's just a blue round wrecked like i i could handle that and i think yeah which is but it's fine like it's number five in productivity not doing so bad i think you're pretty i think you're pretty good icon designer actually yeah you know and i think but it's to the point of like i think it's it's easy enough to like if you if you try to learn basic design and get competent at the basics, you can go that can take you a very long way.

339
00:30:01,840 --> 00:30:09,760
And I think really elegant, new, fancy design that's doing really like groundbreaking or cool things with fancy animations and all that stuff.

340
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:12,320
Like I love it when I am using an app that app that does that.

341
00:30:12,880 --> 00:30:18,800
But that kind of design, um, like that takes a tremendous toll on your development process.

342
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:32,320
And I think a, like a, if you're a thoughtful developer who is willing to put in the work to just kind of like study what the basics of design are, you know, you can get good enough that you can do a lot of it yourself.

343
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:34,960
And I think that's something that has worked really well for me.

344
00:30:35,520 --> 00:30:41,200
Um, and I think it's also been to my benefit that it isn't necessarily that I'm not waiting on a designer.

345
00:30:41,360 --> 00:30:50,240
It is that I'm able to, I'm a better developer because I understand, I took the time to study what makes a good design for an app.

346
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:59,920
And so I'm that informs my development and then it allows me to build things that will be, you know, that are structured in such that the design will naturally flow from it.

347
00:31:00,160 --> 00:31:20,880
And those types of differences that if I just was being handed a list, like here's a handful of mockups, go and build it, and I don't really understand why things are structured the way they are, then I would often find myself in kind of, I'd paint myself into technical corners that if you, if you are responsible for both the design and the development, you're that the two are blending together really well.

348
00:31:21,200 --> 00:31:24,320
And so I think it's something that I certainly recommend.

349
00:31:24,480 --> 00:31:25,360
And I think like.

350
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:29,280
I mean, some of the best apps, I think, have come out of the one developer, one designer teams.

351
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:31,200
I think that is a can be a useful model.

352
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:57,520
But for me, it's just something that I think, you know, in the same way that often I've, you know, I've known many designers who learned just enough coding to be able to sort of to make the basics of the key, the same thing can go the other way that a developer who puts in a little bit of time and is a student of what, like, if you're using something and you start paying attention to why is this good and you don't try and overreach and like try and do things that are beyond your capability.

353
00:31:57,680 --> 00:32:00,160
Like I can make a really nice clean UI.

